# Operating rules

## Project

> **Adopter note:** declare your product here — what it is, what's in scope,
> what's retired. The two trees below are the convention this system expects.

| Tree | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `app/` | The new code (web, desktop, mobile, ops, docs). All new work goes here. |
| `legacy/` | The previous implementation. A **feature and behavior reference**: which features exist and how they behave. Not the look (`07-product-transfer.mdc`). Do not copy god-files, boot DDL or dual-DB. |

## Precedence

1. The user's current message.
2. These rules (`rules/`).
3. Notes in task files, plans and docs. **Older notes that contradict these rules are superseded** — e.g. task files that say "do not start the dev server" (running it is allowed) or "match the legacy look pixel-for-pixel" (the design target is the look).

If a tool's speed or summary defaults conflict with the above, follow the above. Say so in one short line if you had to choose.

